    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Source+Sans+3:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,600;0,700;0,800;1,400;1,600&family=Instrument+Serif:ital@0;1&family=Permanent+Marker&display=swap"
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Nav />

    <div data-zoom-group data-zoom-scan>
      <section class="hero-banner">
        <img data-tilt src={img('01.webp')} alt="Two SureCall EZ-5G Signal Test app screens on a green background, showing a signal-strength check and the SureCall wordmark" />
      </section>

      <section class="marquee-section" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="marquee-row">
          <div class="marquee-track marquee-track-left">
            {[...marqueeWords, ...marqueeWords].map((w) => <span>{w}</span>)}
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="marquee-row">
          <div class="marquee-track marquee-track-right">
            {[...marqueeWords, ...marqueeWords].map((w) => <span>{w}</span>)}
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="marquee-row">
          <div class="marquee-track marquee-track-left">
            {[...marqueeWords, ...marqueeWords].map((w) => <span>{w}</span>)}
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="marquee-row">
          <div class="marquee-track marquee-track-right">
            {[...marqueeWords, ...marqueeWords].map((w) => <span>{w}</span>)}
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="marquee-phone">
          <div class="phone-frame">
            <video class="phone-video" src={`${base}images/surecall/opening.mp4`} autoplay muted loop playsinline aria-label="SureCall app opening screen with an animated signal waveform"></video>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="head-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="head-top">
            <h1 class="title">SureCall</h1>
            <div class="context-box">
              <p class="context-label">Where this started</p>
              <h2 class="context-heading">A booster in the wrong spot is a paperweight</h2>
              <p>SureCall builds cell signal boosters, and teamed up with Verizon on a phone app that helps you work out where to put one. It does three things: test the signal where you are standing, confirm the booster is working once it is mounted, and explain enough about 5G UW that the numbers start to mean something. All of that happens in a garage or a crawlspace, so it had to be <strong>fast, readable, and hard to get wrong</strong>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <dl class="meta">
            {meta.map((m) => (
              <div>
                <dt>{m.label}</dt>
                <dd>{Array.isArray(m.value) ? m.value.map((v) => <span>{v}</span>) : m.value}</dd>
              </div>
            ))}
          </dl>

          <p class="intro">Boosters go into garages, basements and rural houses where the signal was already bad, which is the whole reason somebody buys one. The people installing them split into two groups that want opposite things: technicians who do this all day and want the raw number, and homeowners who will do it exactly once and want to be told whether they are finished. <em>I had to serve the second group without slowing down the first.</em> Verizon wanted fewer support calls, and <strong>a support call is usually just somebody who could not tell whether the thing was working</strong>.</p>

          <p class="pull-quote" data-typewriter>
            <span aria-hidden="true"><span class="tw-seg" data-full="How do you tell somebody "></span><span class="tw-seg pull-quote-highlight" data-full="the install actually worked"></span><span class="tw-seg" data-full=", without teaching them what dBm means?"></span></span>
            <span class="sr-only">How do you tell somebody the install actually worked, without teaching them what dBm means?</span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="stat-band">
        <div class="location-block">
          <p class="location-label">Project Location</p>
          <p class="location-name">Silicon Valley, California</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="dark-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="challenge-head">
            <span class="quirky quirky-blue">Signal data</span>
            <h2>Nobody knows what minus 80 dBm means, including me at first</h2>
          </div>
          <ol class="challenge-grid">
            {challenges.map((c, i) => (
              <li class:list={['challenge-card', 'challenge-card-blue', { 'is-active': i === 0 }]} data-tilt>
                <span class="challenge-num">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
                <p>{c}</p>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="white-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <h2>I never met a user, and I am not going to pretend otherwise</h2>
          <p>I did not run my own research on this one. What I had was a brief from the SureCall and Verizon project managers, and it was specific: most customers have no mental model for what a good or bad dBm value is, <span class="callout-phrase">people want to "see it work" in real time before they believe it</span>, and any instructions have to be <strong>skimmable, with the detail tucked underneath</strong>. We built two personas off that brief so the screens had somebody to answer to. Here is what I learned doing it: a persona built from a client brief is a weaker instrument than one built from interviews. It tells you what the business believes about its customers. <em>It still beat designing for myself</em>, which is what happens when you skip the step entirely.</p>
          <p class="take">
            <span class="take-label">What I think about this stage</span>
            Having no research is not the same as having no user, and I think student work usually gets
            this backwards. It either invents findings it never collected, or it shrugs and designs for
            nobody in particular. <strong>The honest third option is to name the assumption out loud and
            let somebody argue with it.</strong> Everything on this page traces back to a line in that
            brief, which at least makes me wrong in a way you can check.
          </p>
          <div class="image-row image-row-personas">
            <img data-tilt src={img('03.webp')} alt="User persona: Sarah Scott, 38, a remote marketing worker in Wisconsin installing her first signal booster, with her goals, pain points, and needs from the app" />
            <img data-tilt src={img('04.webp')} alt="User persona: Jamal Ortiz, 29, a field technician in Texas who installs boosters professionally, with his goals, pain points, and needs from the app" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="white-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <p class="eyebrow-label">Deciding what earns a place on the screen</p>
          <p>This page has one job: tell you whether the install worked. So the question for every element on it was whether it helped answer that, or whether it just made the page look informed. <strong>Most of it did not survive.</strong> What is left is the handful of things I could not argue away.</p>
          <p class="take">
            <span class="take-label">What I think about this stage</span>
            Deciding what to remove is the actual job. Adding is easy and it feels productive, because
            every addition can be justified on its own. <strong>I have never regretted taking something
            off a screen. I have regretted keeping things on nearly every project I have worked on.</strong>
          </p>
          <div class="image-row-single image-row-single-wide">
            <img data-tilt src={img('09.webp')} alt="Two iteration options for the signal-test page: Option 1 with Test Again and Learn More buttons, and Option 2 showing an automatic rescan with a Close button" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-band">
        <div class="feature-media">
          <img data-tilt src={img('13.webp')} alt="Two SureCall screens showing the signal search state and the color coded Great signal-strength result" />
        </div>
        <div class="feature-text">
          <h2 class="feature-heading">Turning minus 80 dBm into the word Good</h2>
          <p>A color coded meter with plain labels ("Good", "Great") does the translating, so nobody has to learn what dBm means to find out whether they are done. Big tap targets and one step per screen keep it usable with a thumb. The app <strong>rescans on its own once the booster is installed</strong> rather than waiting for you to press "Test Again", because the second you finish mounting it is exactly when you want that number. "Close" sends you back to the home screen instead of leaving you stuck on a results page. And <em>the raw RSRP value stays on screen for the technician who does want the real reading</em>. Plain language for one person, the data for the other, same screen, no mode switch.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="dark-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="challenge-head">
            <span class="quirky quirky-sage">Plain language</span>
            <h2>Teaching 5G without handing anyone a manual</h2>
          </div>
          <ol class="challenge-grid">
            {challenges.map((c, i) => (
              <li class:list={['challenge-card', 'challenge-card-sage', { 'is-active': i === 1 }]} data-tilt>
                <span class="challenge-num">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
                <p>{c}</p>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="white-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="image-row-single image-row-single-wide">
            <img data-tilt src={img('08.webp')} alt="Three iteration options for explaining 5G C-Band and UW technology: plain information with no aesthetic, relevant information in a gradient bubble, and relevant information with color coded signal specifics" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-band feature-band-reverse">
        <div class="feature-media">
          <img data-tilt src={img('14.webp')} alt="Three SureCall screens guiding a user to move near a window, checking 5G UW strength, and offering booster tips" />
        </div>
        <div class="feature-text">
          <h2 class="feature-heading">You should know it worked before you climb down</h2>
          <p>The test closes the loop in a few seconds, so you are not standing on a ladder wondering whether to take the whole thing back down. These installs happen in the worst rooms in the house, so <strong>a clear pass or fail mattered more than a beautiful readout</strong>. The mid fidelity rounds leaned on the <em>aesthetic usability effect</em>: a calm, uncluttered screen reads as trustworthy before anyone has read a word on it. In a dark garage, that first impression is most of what you get.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="dark-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="challenge-head">
            <span class="quirky quirky-coral">Field use</span>
            <h2>Built for a basement, one hand, and bad light</h2>
          </div>
          <ol class="challenge-grid">
            {challenges.map((c, i) => (
              <li class:list={['challenge-card', 'challenge-card-coral', { 'is-active': i === 2 }]} data-tilt>
                <span class="challenge-num">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
                <p>{c}</p>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="white-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <h2>Sketches first, because they are cheap to be wrong in</h2>
          <p>With the brief from my project manager and Verizon in hand, I sketched rough concepts to work out <strong>the flow, the screens, and which features earned their place</strong>. They were fast to draw and easy to lay side by side, which is the whole point. I would much rather throw out six sketches than one prototype.</p>
          <p class="take">
            <span class="take-label">What I think about this stage</span>
            Client work changed how I sketch. When somebody is paying you, there is real pressure to
            turn up with something polished, and polished too early is how you end up defending a
            direction instead of testing one. I started bringing three rough options rather than one good
            one, and the conversations got better immediately.
            <strong>Nobody argues with a drawing that is obviously a draft.</strong>
          </p>
          <div class="image-row-single image-row-single-wide">
            <img data-tilt src={img('07.webp')} alt="Low-fidelity wireframes for the SureCall app" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="white-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <p class="eyebrow-label">How it ended up</p>
          <div class="image-row-single image-row-single-phone">
            <video class="prototype-video" src={`${base}images/surecall/prototype.mp4`} autoplay muted loop playsinline aria-label="Walkthrough of the final SureCall prototype, from the signal-strength check through booster setup"></video>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="white-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <p class="eyebrow-label">The kit it is built from</p>
          <div class="image-row-single image-row-single-wide">
            <img data-tilt src={img('12.webp')} alt="SureCall design kit: typography scale, color palette, and logo and icon assets" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="white-block white-block-flush-bottom">
        <div class="image-row-single">
          <img data-tilt src={img('02.webp')} alt="Collage of SureCall app screens arranged at an angle, showing the signal test, booster setup, and information flows" />
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="dark-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <h2>Where it landed, and what I would change</h2>
          <p>This is the project where I learned that the screen is not the whole interface. The garage is part of the interface too. Bad light, a ladder, a phone in one hand: <em>designing for that made me cut things I was fond of</em>, and the app is better for it.</p>
          <p>Working at a small company meant I got to be hands on with every step, which is not something I would have gotten somewhere larger. I came out of it with better design instincts and, unexpectedly, a working knowledge of cellular boosters. The part I valued most was sitting with the backend engineers and watching what actually gets built. They would tell me to change or add things based on <strong>how easy or hard an element was to code</strong>, which was humbling at first and then just useful. Thank you SureCall for having me.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="dark-block">
        <div class="wrap">
          <h2 class="takeaways-heading">What I took with me</h2>
          <div class="takeaways-grid">
            {takeaways.map((t) => (
              <div class="takeaway-card">
                <span class="takeaway-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <h3>{t.title}</h3>
                <p>{t.body}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="up-next">
        <div class="wrap">
          <span class="quirky quirky-blue">Up Next</span>
          <a class="up-next-row" href={nextProject.href} data-tilt>
            <img src={nextProject.image} alt="" />
            <div>
              <h2>{nextProject.title}</h2>
              <p>{nextProject.subtitle}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="btn-outline">View Project</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <Footer />

    <Lightbox />

    <script>
      import '../../scripts/site.js';
      import '../../scripts/lightbox.js';

      const btn = document.querySelector('[data-copy-email]');
      btn?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText('julianliaowork@gmail.com');
          const original = btn.textContent;
          btn.textContent = 'Copied!';
          setTimeout(() => { btn.textContent = original; }, 1500);
        } catch {
          window.location.href = 'mailto:julianliaowork@gmail.com';
        }
      });

      // Belt-and-suspenders: the autoplay/muted/loop/playsinline attributes
      // already handle this in every modern browser, but some browsers
      // silently drop a programmatic play() if it's called before the
      // element is attached — this re-triggers it once the page is ready.
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLVideoElement>('.phone-video, .prototype-video').forEach((v) => {
        v.play().catch(() => {});
      });

      // Typewriter effect on the pull-quote — types each segment in order
      // (plain text, then the highlighted phrase, then the trailing plain
      // text) once the quote scrolls into view. Reduced-motion and
      // no-IntersectionObserver both fall back to showing the full text.
      const quoteEl = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-typewriter]');
      if (quoteEl) {
        const segments = Array.from(quoteEl.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.tw-seg'));
        const reduced = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

        const typeSegments = () => {
          let segIndex = 0;
          let charIndex = 0;
          const step = () => {
            if (segIndex >= segments.length) return;
            const seg = segments[segIndex];
            const full = seg.dataset.full ?? '';
            if (charIndex <= full.length) {
              seg.textContent = full.slice(0, charIndex);
              charIndex++;
              setTimeout(step, 28);
            } else {
              segIndex++;
              charIndex = 0;
              setTimeout(step, 28);
            }
          };
          step();
        };

        if (reduced || !('IntersectionObserver' in window)) {
          segments.forEach((seg) => { seg.textContent = seg.dataset.full ?? ''; });
        } else {
          const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries, obs) => {
            entries.forEach((entry) => {
              if (entry.isIntersecting) {
                typeSegments();
                obs.disconnect();
              }
            });
          }, { threshold: 0.4 });
          io.observe(quoteEl);
        }
      }
    </script>

    <style>
      :global(body) {
        background: #ffffff;
      }



      .wrap {
        max-width: 74rem;
        margin-inline: auto;
        padding-inline: clamp(1.25rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
      }

      /* Nav ------------------------------------------------------------ */




      .btn-pill {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        border: 1px solid var(--ink);
        border-radius: 999px;
        padding: 0.6em 1.4em;
        text-decoration: none;
        color: var(--ink);
        background: transparent;
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 600;
        cursor: pointer;
      }

      .btn-pill-solid {
        background: var(--ink);
        color: var(--bg);
      }

      /* Hero banner ------------------------------------------------------- */
      .hero-banner {
        aspect-ratio: 8 / 3;
        overflow: hidden;
      }

      .hero-banner img {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
        object-fit: cover;
        object-position: center;
      }

      /* Marquee ----------------------------------------------------------- */
      .marquee-section {
        position: relative;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        justify-content: space-around;
        min-height: clamp(380px, 48vw, 640px);
        padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
        overflow: hidden;
        background: #ffffff;
      }

      .marquee-row {
        overflow: hidden;
        white-space: nowrap;
      }

      .marquee-track {
        display: inline-flex;
        width: max-content;
      }

      .marquee-track span {
        display: inline-block;
        padding-inline: 1.5rem;
        font-family: var(--font-display);
        font-weight: 400;
        font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 5vw, 3rem);
        color: #4fd8ae;
        white-space: nowrap;
      }

      .marquee-row:nth-child(odd) .marquee-track span {
        color: rgba(79, 216, 174, 0.55);
      }

      .marquee-track-left {
        animation: marquee-left 32s linear infinite;
      }

      .marquee-track-right {
        animation: marquee-right 32s linear infinite;
      }

      @keyframes marquee-left {
        from { transform: translateX(0); }
        to { transform: translateX(-50%); }
      }

      @keyframes marquee-right {
        from { transform: translateX(-50%); }
        to { transform: translateX(0); }
      }

      .marquee-phone {
        position: absolute;
        top: 50%;
        left: 50%;
        transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
        z-index: 5;
      }

      .phone-frame {
        width: clamp(140px, 16vw, 220px);
        aspect-ratio: 658 / 1396;
        border: 3px solid var(--ink);
        border-radius: 1.5rem;
        padding: 0.5rem;
        background: var(--bg);
      }

      .phone-frame .placeholder {
        height: 100%;
        aspect-ratio: auto;
        border-radius: 1rem;
      }

      .phone-video {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
        object-fit: cover;
        border-radius: 1rem;
      }

      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .marquee-track-left,
        .marquee-track-right {
          animation: none;
        }
      }

      /* Head block -------------------------------------------------------- */
      .head-block {
        padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem) clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
      }

      .head-top {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        gap: 1.5rem;
        align-items: start;
        margin-bottom: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
      }

      .title {
        font-family: var(--font-display);
        font-weight: 400;
        font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 10vw, 7rem);
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
        line-height: 0.98;
        color: var(--ink);
        margin: 0;
      }

      /* Fill matches the section background on purpose — the reference
         had this as a plain white box floating on the page's cream
         background, which read as a mismatched card rather than part
         of the page. */
      .context-box {
        background: transparent;
        border-left: 3px solid var(--line-strong);
        padding-left: 1.25rem;
      }

      .context-label {
        margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
        color: var(--ink-faint);
      }

      .context-heading {
        margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
        font-family: var(--font-display);
        font-weight: 400;
        font-size: 1.3rem;
        color: var(--ink);
      }

      .context-box p:not(.context-label) {
        margin: 0;
        max-width: none;
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
      }

      @media (min-width: 800px) {
        .head-top { grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; }
      }

      .meta {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(10rem, 1fr));
        gap: 1.5rem;
        padding-bottom: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
        margin: 0 0 clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
      }

      .meta dt {
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        color: var(--ink-faint);
        margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
      }

      .meta dd {
        margin: 0;
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 700;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        color: var(--ink);
      }

      .meta dd span {
        display: block;
      }

      .intro {
        max-width: none;
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
        text-align: justify;
        text-align-last: left;
        hyphens: auto;
      }

      .pull-quote {
        position: relative;
        max-width: none;
        font-family: var(--font-serif);
        font-weight: 400;
        font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3.4vw, 2.4rem);
        line-height: 1.4;
        color: var(--ink-faint);
        margin-top: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
        text-align: center;
      }

      .pull-quote-highlight {
        color: #06251e;
        font-weight: 700;
        box-shadow: inset 0 -0.35em 0 rgba(0, 179, 133, 0.22);
      }

      .pull-quote[data-typewriter]::after {
        content: '';
        display: inline-block;
        width: 2px;
        height: 1em;
        margin-left: 2px;
        background: currentColor;
        vertical-align: text-bottom;
        animation: pull-quote-blink 0.9s steps(1) infinite;
      }

      @keyframes pull-quote-blink {
        50% { opacity: 0; }
      }

      .sr-only {
        position: absolute;
        width: 1px;
        height: 1px;
        padding: 0;
        margin: -1px;
        overflow: hidden;
        clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
        white-space: nowrap;
        border: 0;
      }

      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .pull-quote[data-typewriter]::after {
          animation: none;
        }
      }

      /* By the numbers ------------------------------------------------------- */
      .stat-band {
        background: #00b38a;
        color: #fdfbf9;
        padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
      }

      .location-block {
        text-align: center;
        padding-inline: clamp(1.25rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
      }

      .location-label {
        margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
        color: #fdfbf9;
      }

      .location-name {
        margin: 0;
        font-family: var(--font-display);
        font-weight: 400;
        font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3.5rem);
        line-height: 1.1;
        color: #fdfbf9;
      }

      /* Dark / white blocks ---------------------------------------------- */
      .dark-block {
        background: var(--ink);
        color: var(--bg);
        padding-block: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem);
      }

      .white-block {
        padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
      }

      .white-block-flush-bottom {
        padding-bottom: 0;
      }

      .white-block h2 {
        font-family: var(--font-display);
        font-weight: 400;
        font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
        margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
        color: var(--ink);
      }

      .dark-block h2 {
        font-family: var(--font-display);
        font-weight: 400;
        font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
        margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
      }

      .white-block p {
        max-width: none;
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
        text-align: justify;
        text-align-last: left;
        hyphens: auto;
      }

      .dark-block .wrap > p {
        max-width: none;
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: rgba(253, 251, 249, 0.7);
        text-align: justify;
        text-align-last: left;
        hyphens: auto;
      }


      /* Typographic emphasis experiment — bold marks a design decision,
         italic marks an insight/rationale, and .callout-phrase (used once,
         on the single clearest insight on the page) bumps size + color for
         a magazine-pull-quote-within-a-paragraph effect. */
      .white-block strong,
      .context-box strong,
      .feature-text strong {
        color: var(--ink);
        font-weight: 700;
      }

      .dark-block strong {
        color: var(--bg);
        font-weight: 700;
      }

      .white-block em,
      .context-box em,
      .feature-text em {
        font-style: italic;
        color: var(--ink);
      }

      .dark-block em {
        font-style: italic;
        color: var(--bg);
      }

      .callout-phrase {
        font-size: 1.2em;
        font-weight: 700;
        color: #00b385;
      }

      .eyebrow-label {
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 700;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        color: #00b385;
        margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
      }

      /* Images ------------------------------------------------------------ */
      .image-row {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        gap: 1.5rem;
        margin-top: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
      }

      .image-row img {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
      }

      @media (min-width: 700px) {
        .image-row-personas { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
      }

      .image-row-single {
        margin-top: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
      }

      .image-row-single-wide {
        max-width: 56rem;
        margin-inline: auto;
      }

      .image-row-single img {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
      }

      .image-row-single-phone {
        max-width: 20rem;
        margin-inline: auto;
      }

      .prototype-video {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        aspect-ratio: 912 / 1800;
        border-radius: 1.5rem;
      }

      .placeholder {
        display: grid;
        place-items: center;
        aspect-ratio: 21 / 9;
        border: 1px dashed var(--line-strong);
        background: #ffffff;
        color: var(--ink-faint);
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.1em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
      }

      .placeholder-phone {
        aspect-ratio: 9 / 19;
      }

      /* Feature bands (green, full-bleed) --------------------------------- */
      .feature-band {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        background: #00b38a;
      }

      .feature-media img {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
        object-fit: cover;
      }

      .feature-text {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        justify-content: center;
        padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
      }

      .feature-heading {
        font-family: var(--font-serif);
        font-weight: 400;
        font-style: italic;
        font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.1rem);
        color: var(--ink);
        margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
      }

      /* Fill matches the section background on purpose — same fix as the
         context box above; the reference had a white card sitting on
         this green band. */
      .feature-text p {
        margin: 0;
        max-width: none;
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: rgba(6, 37, 30, 0.75);
      }

      @media (min-width: 800px) {
        .feature-band { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
        .feature-band-reverse .feature-media { order: 2; }
        .feature-band-reverse .feature-text { order: 1; }
      }

      /* Challenge cards --------------------------------------------------- */
      .challenge-head {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 1.1rem;
        margin-bottom: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
      }

      .challenge-head .quirky {
        margin-top: -0.2rem;
      }

      .challenge-head h2 {
        color: var(--bg);
        margin: 0;
      }

      .quirky {
        font-family: var(--font-quirky);
        font-size: 1.2rem;
        transform: rotate(-3deg);
        display: inline-block;
      }

      /* All three challenge sections (and Up Next) share one accent now —
         SureCall's own brand green (#00B385, from the Design Kit asset)
         instead of the earlier blue/sage/coral rotation. */
      .quirky-blue,
      .quirky-sage,
      .quirky-coral {
        color: #00b385;
      }

      .challenge-grid {
        list-style: none;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        gap: 1rem;
      }

      .challenge-card {
        --tilt-x: 0deg;
        --tilt-y: 0deg;
        border: 1px solid rgba(253, 251, 249, 0.15);
        border-left: 3px solid rgba(253, 251, 249, 0.15);
        padding: 1.5rem;
        background: rgba(253, 251, 249, 0.03);
        transform: perspective(700px) rotateX(var(--tilt-x)) rotateY(var(--tilt-y));
        transition: background 0.3s ease, border-color 0.3s ease, transform 0.3s var(--ease-out);
      }

      .challenge-card p {
        margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
        max-width: none;
        color: rgba(253, 251, 249, 0.45);
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }

      .challenge-num {
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 800;
        font-size: 1.5rem;
        color: rgba(253, 251, 249, 0.35);
      }

      .challenge-card.is-active {
        background: rgba(253, 251, 249, 0.08);
        border-color: rgba(253, 251, 249, 0.3);
      }

      .challenge-card-blue.is-active,
      .challenge-card-sage.is-active,
      .challenge-card-coral.is-active {
        border-left-color: #00b385;
      }

      .challenge-card-blue.is-active .challenge-num,
      .challenge-card-sage.is-active .challenge-num,
      .challenge-card-coral.is-active .challenge-num {
        color: #00b385;
      }

      .challenge-card.is-active p {
        color: var(--bg);
        font-weight: 500;
      }

      @media (min-width: 700px) {
        .challenge-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
      }

      /* Key takeaways ------------------------------------------------------- */
      .takeaways-heading { color: var(--bg); }

      .takeaways-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        gap: 1.5rem;
        margin-top: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
        padding-top: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
        border-top: 1px solid rgba(253, 251, 249, 0.15);
      }

      .takeaway-card {
        padding-left: 0;
      }

      .takeaway-dot {
        display: inline-block;
        width: 24px;
        height: 24px;
        border-radius: 999px;
        background: var(--accent-light);
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
      }

      .takeaway-card h3 {
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        color: var(--bg);
        margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
      }

      .takeaway-card p {
        margin: 0;
        max-width: none;
        color: rgba(253, 251, 249, 0.6);
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }

      @media (min-width: 700px) {
        .takeaways-grid {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
        }

        .takeaways-grid .takeaway-card:last-child {
          border-left: 1px solid rgba(253, 251, 249, 0.15);
          padding-left: 2rem;
        }
      }

      /* Up next --------------------------------------------------------------- */
      .up-next { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem); }

      .up-next-row {
        --tilt-x: 0deg;
        --tilt-y: 0deg;
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 1.5rem;
        margin-top: 1rem;
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      .up-next-row img {
        width: 100px;
        aspect-ratio: 1;
        object-fit: cover;
        border: 1px solid var(--line);
        transform: perspective(700px) rotateX(var(--tilt-x)) rotateY(var(--tilt-y));
        transition: transform 0.3s var(--ease-out);
      }

      .up-next-row h2 {
        margin: 0;
        font-family: var(--font-display);
        font-weight: 400;
        font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.2rem);
        color: var(--ink);
      }

      .up-next-row p {
        margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
        color: var(--ink-faint);
        font-size: 0.9rem;
      }

      .btn-outline {
        margin-left: auto;
        border: 1px solid var(--ink);
        border-radius: 999px;
        padding: 0.5em 1.2em;
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        color: var(--ink);
      }

      /* Footer ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
      .footer { text-align: center; }

      .footer-heading {
        color: var(--bg);
        font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 4.5rem);
        font-family: var(--font-display);
        font-weight: 400;
      }

      .footer-actions {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        justify-content: center;
        gap: 1rem;
        margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
      }

      .footer .btn-pill { border-color: var(--bg); color: var(--bg); }
      .footer .btn-pill-solid { background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); }

      .footer-social {
        color: rgba(253, 251, 249, 0.7);
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-weight: 600;
        text-decoration: none;
      }
    
      /* Opinion asides — my running commentary on each stage, set apart
         from the account of what happened. */
      .take {
        max-width: 60ch;
        margin: 2rem 0 0;
        padding-left: 1.1rem;
        border-left: 3px solid #00b385;
        font-family: var(--font-body);
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
      }

      .take strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 700; }

      .take-label {
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
        font-family: var(--font-quirky);
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        color: #00b385;
      }
</style>
  </body>
</html>
